  callers="CALLERS: `verifyTransaction` is reached from `POST /api/nft/record` (`recordClientMint`) and `POST /api/nft/verify/transaction` (nft.routes.ts); `getClient` only from `verifyTransaction`/`verifyAsset`. WHAT AN ORDINARY ERROR GETS (the rule for taking the site): an ordinary Blockfrost error at lookup answers `{ verified:false, status:'error', error:<message> }`, `/record` answers 201 `onChainVerified:false` and stores ONE `pending` row with the caller's own tx hash (minted_at null); an ordinary init error answers `{ verified:false, status:'pending' }` and the same 201 and pending row (QA gate 109 measured all of this with the real router, `recordClientMint` and winston). Today (a hostile non-string message, identical at base and PR 1927) with the real logger: `/record` answers 500 and stores NOTHING, `/verify/transaction` answers 500. After: exactly the ordinary row, with the constant reason. No outcome kind is new, because an unreadable-getter value already gets this answer from PR 1927. Never verified: no path answers `verified:true` without a resolved chain lookup. **BEHAVIOUR CHANGE the raise PR must state, with its PERSISTED-STATE consequence:** for a hostile non-string message only, `POST /api/nft/record` now stores ONE `pending` row (caller-supplied tx hash NOT verified on chain, exactly as an ordinary Blockfrost error, a 404 or an unconfigured key already store) and answers 201, instead of 500 with nothing stored; the other hostile shapes (a message whose `toString` throws, a null-prototype message) already persisted a pending row but echoed `error: {}`, and now echo the constant `unreadable thrown value`. Recommended TIER 1 (the persisted state changes for the revoked-Proxy-message value).",
